  n = valid reps of 3 (VPN_FAIL / ZERO_BW / NO_LANE excluded; see CSV).
  sp o/n = reps that used a single path (off/on), counted not excluded —
     expected for minrtt at low P: a single flow does not stripe across paths.
  gain% is the intended hybrid A/B, NOT pure lane efficiency: the RAW (off)
     baseline also pays the datagram packet-reorder penalty (a single TCP
     flow striped across two 25ms legs backs off on reorder), which the
     in-order STREAM lane avoids — so gain% widens as fewer flows spread load.
